eek, Dry Gulch, Gold\nCreek, Cook Creek, Gove Creek, West Kiowa Creek, East Cherry\nCreek, Lake Gulch, Antelope Creek, Plum Creek, Wildcat Creek,\nCherry Creek, Turkey Creek, East Plum Creek, West Creek, Bear\nCreek, Wolf Creek, Running Creek, Carpenter Creek, Willow Creek,\nDry Creek, Spring Creek, West Cherry Creek, Kiowa Creek and\nFourmile Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are\nexpected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nElbert, Larkspur, Greenland, Perry Park, Westcreek and Cheesman\nReservoir.","ends":"2026-08-13T23:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a2e3575bf0d730a880a7d7a6f327433b352f9116.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a2e3575bf0d730a880a7d7a6f327433b352f9116.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-14T00:27:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 140027 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 627 PM MDT Thu Aug 13 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Localized flash flooding possible due to heavy rain producing thunderstorms. Highest risk is over the eastern Colorado plains, where a Flood Watch is in effect from 3 pm to 10 pm. - Another round of storms Friday afternoon/evening with a continued threat o","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-13T19:26:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Friday...Monsoonal moisture will remain high across the area through Friday, with numerous showers and storms with wetting rainfall. Heavy rainfall rates may lead to localized flash flooding, particularly over burn scars and the eastern Colorado plains. Humidity readings will be high and temperatures will be several degrees cooler than normal during the day. LON","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/produc